const e={bergamot:["Bright and bitter-sweet, like a sunlit peel with a soft floral, faintly tea-like edge.","Its oil is what flavours Earl Grey tea, sprayed onto the black tea leaves."],lemon:["Sharp, sparkling and squeaky-clean, a sour yellow flash that fades within minutes.","Squeezed over fish and pancakes, sliced into drinks, and the default scent of washing-up liquid."],mandarin:["Soft, juicy and almost candied, a gentle sugary tang with a faintly herbal, aromatic twist.","Small, loose-skinned and easy to segment, it is the fruit traditionally tucked into the toe of a Christmas stocking."],orange:["Round, juicy and sunny, like tearing open a ripe fruit, cheerful but quick to fade.","The everyday breakfast juice in the carton, and the flavour of Jaffa Cakes and chocolate segment balls."],grapefruit:["Tart, juicy and slightly bitter, with a sulphurous, almost sweaty tang that feels sparkling and modern.","A large breakfast fruit often halved and sprinkled with sugar, famous for clashing with certain medicines."],lime:["Zingy, green and sharp, with a fizzy, slightly bitter edge like a freshly cut wedge.","Squeezed into margaritas and mojitos, and once given to British sailors to ward off scurvy."],yuzu:["Tart and floral, somewhere between grapefruit and mandarin, with a clean, aromatic freshness.","A knobbly East Asian fruit floated in hot baths at the winter solstice and squeezed into ponzu sauce."],petitgrain:["Green, bitter and slightly woody, a crisp herbal freshness with a faint neroli-like floral lilt.","A classic eau de cologne staple, from the same bitter Seville tree that also gives neroli and marmalade fruit."],kumquat:["Tangy and bittersweet, a bright, tart zing balanced by a candied, honeyed sweetness.","Tiny oval fruits eaten whole, skin and all, and given as lucky gifts at Lunar New Year."],cedrat:["Sharp, clean and dry, a lemon-like brightness that is greener, more resinous and less sugary.","A huge, knobbly, thick-skinned ancestor of the lemon, candied for panettone and held as the etrog at Sukkot."],pomelo:["Mild, juicy and gently bitter, like a softer, sweeter grapefruit with a watery freshness.","The largest fruit of its family, with a thick spongy rind, and one of the two parents of grapefruit."],calamansi:["Sour and sparkling, a tart green tang with a hint of sugary tangerine.","A marble-sized green fruit squeezed into soy dipping sauces and over noodles in Southeast Asian kitchens."],clementine:["Sugary, juicy and sunny, a gentle tangy brightness that is softer than a classic breakfast fruit.","A seedless, loose-skinned winter fruit, said to be a chance cross found by a monk in an orphanage garden."],kaffirlime:["Sharp, green and intensely aromatic, a lemongrass-bright tang with a waxy, almost metallic snap.","A staple of Thai cooking, torn into green curries and tom yum soup for its piercing perfume."],litsea:["Sharp, sherbety and lemony, like lemon sherbet sweets with a green, slightly peppery edge.","An Asian relative of the laurel whose oil is a cheap natural source of citral, the lemon-scented molecule."],blacklime:["Sour, smoky and fermented, a tangy fruitiness turned dark, earthy and slightly musty.","A hard, hollow, dark brown ball cracked into Persian and Gulf stews to add a deep sourness."],fingerlime:["Tart, bright and crunchy-fresh, like tiny bursting beads of sour juice with a herbal edge.","A slender rainforest fruit packed with pearl-like vesicles that pop like roe, spooned onto oysters."],neroli:["Honeyed, green and luminous, a clean bridal floral with a bitter, slightly soapy freshness.","Brides traditionally wore its waxy buds in their hair, and its floral water flavours Middle Eastern pastries."],rose:["Lush, honeyed and velvety, the classic romantic floral with a lemony lift and a hint of clove.","It flavours Turkish delight and Middle Eastern sweets, and its hips make a vitamin-rich syrup."],rose_centifolia:["Soft, honeyed and slightly green, a delicate, airy floral with a waxy, peppery sweetness.","Nicknamed after a leafy vegetable for its plump, tightly packed heads, it crowds Dutch Golden Age still lifes."],rose_turkey:["Deep, jammy and spicy, a rich red floral with honey, clove and a slightly fruity warmth.","The same species as the classic attar bloom, hand-picked at dawn before the sun burns off its scent."],jasmine:["Heady, warm and narcotic, a creamy floral with a fruity sweetness and an animalic, indolic edge.","A climbing shrub with tiny starry blooms, picked by hand at dawn while their scent is at its strongest."],sambac:["Green, fruity and heady, a lush white floral with a ripe banana-like sweetness and a tea-like freshness.","The national flower of the Philippines, strung into temple garlands and used to scent Chinese green tea."],tuberose:["Creamy, buttery and intoxicating, a heavy white floral with a camphor-green coolness and rubbery sweetness.","Its tall spikes of waxy blooms are strung into wedding garlands, and its scent is strongest after dark."],ylang:["Lush, creamy and banana-sweet, a tropical floral with a custardy richness and a faint medicinal spice.","Droopy, ribbon-petalled yellow blooms from a tropical tree, a key part of the famous Chanel No. 5."],lotv:["Fresh, dewy and green, a clean bell-like floral with a crisp, slightly lemony springtime sweetness.","Tiny white bells given in sprigs for luck on the first of May, pretty but highly poisonous."],violet:["Powdery, sugary and cosmetic, with a candied, lipstick-like softness and a green, cucumbery edge.","The flavour of old-fashioned purple pastilles and crystallised petals on cakes, a favourite of Victorian ladies."],iris:["Cool, powdery and buttery, like suede, raw carrot and makeup powder, and one of perfumery’s costliest materials.","A gin botanical, once ground into tooth and wig powders; the heraldic fleur-de-lis is thought to depict it."],lavender:["Clean, herbal and calming, with a fresh camphor bite over a soft, hay-like sweetness.","Tucked into sachets in linen drawers, it scents soaps and sleep pillows and turns Mediterranean hillsides purple."],geranium:["Green, minty and rose-like, a sharp, fresh floral with a crisp, metallic, lemony bite.","A common windowsill pot plant whose oil serves as a cheaper stand-in for rose."],peony:["Fresh, airy and rosy, a dewy pink floral with a crisp, slightly fruity and watery sweetness.","Huge, ruffled, short-lived blooms beloved in bridal bouquets and long celebrated as the king of flowers."],osmanthus:["Apricot-sweet and leathery, a golden floral with tea-like, suede and fruity nuances.","Its tiny golden blooms flavour tea, jellies and sweet wine, and perfume East Asian streets in autumn."],mimosa:["Powdery, honeyed and soft, a fluffy yellow floral with a green, slightly almondy, cucumber-like sweetness.","Fluffy yellow pompom blooms sold in late winter and given on International Women’s Day in Italy."],freesia:["Fresh, peppery and lightly fruity, a clean, airy floral with a dewy, almost soapy sweetness.","A funnel-shaped florist’s favourite named after a German doctor, and a staple scent of shower gels."],heliotrope:["Soft, powdery and almondy, like marzipan and cherry pie with a hint of vanilla.","A purple bedding plant nicknamed cherry pie, beloved of Victorian gardeners for its almond-scented clusters."],magnolia:["Creamy, lemony and fresh, a large waxy floral with a soft, clean, slightly fruity sweetness.","Huge waxy blooms from an ancient lineage of trees that evolved before bees and is pollinated by beetles."],frangipani:["Creamy, tropical and sunny, like coconut, peach and apricot wrapped in a soft white floral.","Waxy five-petalled blooms tucked behind the ear and strung into leis across the Pacific and Bali."],gardenia:["Creamy, green and mushroomy, a lush white floral with a buttery, coconutty richness.","Billie Holiday wore its waxy white blooms in her hair; it is also a fussy, glossy-leaved houseplant."],lotus:["Watery, airy and serene, a soft aquatic floral with a powdery, slightly sweet and earthy freshness.","A sacred bloom of Buddhism and Hinduism that rises clean from muddy ponds; its seeds and stems are eaten."],champaca:["Rich, fruity and tea-like, a golden floral with apricot, spice and a heady, slightly leathery depth.","Its orange-gold blooms are offered at temples and threaded into hair, and the tree is sacred to Hindus and Buddhists."],carnation:["Spicy and peppery, a clove-laced floral with a warm, slightly powdery, old-fashioned sweetness.","A frilly florist’s staple worn in buttonholes and on Mother’s Day; Oscar Wilde famously wore a green one."],hyacinth:["Green, cool and heady, a sappy spring floral with an earthy, slightly peppery sweetness.","Grown from fat bulbs forced in glass jars on winter windowsills; in myth it sprang from Apollo’s slain lover."],narcissus:["Green, hay-like and slightly animalic, a heady spring floral with honeyed and faintly leathery depths.","Wordsworth wandered among its springtime host; in myth, a youth who fell for his own reflection became it."],honeysuckle:["Nectar-rich and green, a honeyed summer-evening floral with a fruity, slightly dewy freshness.","A hedgerow climber whose trumpet-shaped blooms children pinch to suck out the drop of nectar."],immortelle:["Warm, honeyed and curry-like, a dry, hay-scented material with a maple-syrup, fenugreek sweetness.","A silvery Mediterranean shrub, also called curry plant, whose papery yellow blooms keep their shape when dried."],tagetes:["Green, fruity and pungent, an apple-like sharpness with a bitter, herbal, slightly rubbery edge.","Orange and golden pompom blooms strung into garlands and heaped on Day of the Dead altars."],chamomile:["Soft, hay-like and apple-sweet, a herbal, honeyed material that feels calm, dry and slightly bitter.","Brewed as a bedtime herbal tea, and used in soothing creams and in rinses to brighten blonde hair."],boronia:["Fruity and violet-like, with raspberry, tea and a dark, slightly woody sweetness.","A small shrub with brown-and-yellow bell-shaped blooms, unusually rich in beta-ionone, the violet molecule."],karokarounde:["Heady, honeyed and spicy, a rich floral with a warm, slightly leathery, fruity depth.","A rare West African savannah shrub in the coffee family whose starry white blooms give an obscure, costly natural."],lily:["Heady, spicy and creamy, a big floral with clove, honey and a faintly green, pollen-dusted richness.","Tall trumpet blooms whose orange pollen stains clothes, a staple of Easter and funerals, and toxic to cats."],lilac:["Fresh, green and almondy, a soft spring floral with a powdery, slightly honeyed sweetness.","Dense purple cone-shaped clusters on a garden shrub in late spring, and a pale purple shade shares its name."],hawthorn:["Almondy, honeyed and slightly animalic, a creamy hedgerow floral with an earthy, faintly fishy edge.","A spiny hedging shrub of country lanes, with red berries in autumn, long thought unlucky to bring indoors."],cyclamen:["Fresh, watery and airy, a cool, translucent floral with a faintly green, lily-like sweetness.","A winter pot plant with swept-back petals like butterflies, grown from a tuber once called sowbread."],sweetpea:["Airy, fruity and delicate, a soft summer floral with honeyed, slightly green and neroli-like nuances.","A climbing annual grown up cane wigwams in cottage gardens and picked often for vases, an Edwardian craze."],waterlily:["Aquatic, airy and cool, a soft floral with a green, slightly powdery and sweet freshness.","Floating pads and blooms that Monet painted over and over in his garden pond at Giverny."],gingerlily:["Fresh, creamy and spicy, a lush tropical floral with a peppery, zesty brightness.","Fluttering, butterfly-shaped blooms on tall leafy canes, from a relative of the knobbly kitchen spice."],datura:["Heady, creamy and narcotic, a lush evening floral with a sweet, slightly lemony and spicy edge.","Huge pendulous bell-shaped blooms hanging from a highly toxic, hallucinogenic shrub of the nightshade family."],broom:["Honeyed and hay-like, a sunny yellow floral with a green, slightly animalic and fruity warmth.","Bright yellow pea-like blooms on rush-like green stems; a related shrub gave an English royal dynasty its name."],cherryblossom:["Soft, powdery and airy, a delicate pink floral with an almondy, faintly fruity sweetness.","Celebrated each spring with picnics under clouds of pale pink trees; Washington’s Tidal Basin is famous for them."],wisteria:["Soft, powdery and grapey, a gentle lilac-like floral with a honeyed, slightly almondy sweetness.","Long cascading lavender-purple clusters that drape pergolas and cottage walls in late spring."],hibiscus:["Tart, fruity and berry-like, a tangy red floral with a cranberry sharpness and light green freshness.","Brews a tart crimson herbal tea, drunk iced as agua de jamaica in Mexico and as karkade in Egypt."],orchid:["Soft, creamy and exotic, a smooth floral with powdery, slightly spicy and vanilla-tinged sweetness.","The supermarket houseplant with long-lasting moth-like blooms, from the plant family that also gives us vanilla."],tiare:["Creamy, sunny and coconutty, a lush tropical floral with a soft, honeyed, slightly spicy richness.","Its starry blooms are steeped in coconut oil to make a South Pacific beauty oil, and worn behind the ear."],stephanotis:["Waxy, creamy and green, a clean white floral with a soft, slightly spicy, lily-like sweetness.","Waxy white star-shaped tubes on a glossy climber, a classic of bridal bouquets and headpieces."],tulip:["Green, cool and faintly fresh, a subtle, sappy floral more like crisp stems than nectar.","Spring bulbs that sparked a 17th-century Dutch speculative mania, when single bulbs changed hands for fortunes."],taifrose:["Spicy, fresh and intensely rich, a dewy, regal floral with lemony brightness and a warm, peppery depth.","Grown on cool highland terraces, it yields one of the costliest attars, sold by the tola as a precious gift."],heather:["Honeyed, earthy and dry, a moorland floral with a hay-like, slightly woody sweetness.","The purple carpet of moors and upland bogs, beloved by bees for a dark, thick, jelly-like honey."],linden:["Honeyed, green and airy, a soft summer floral with a fresh, slightly citrusy, nectar sweetness.","Its dried blooms make the calming tisane into which Proust’s narrator dips his madeleine."],edelweiss:["Cool, airy and clean, an imagined alpine floral with a soft, powdery, slightly honeyed freshness.","A woolly white star of high mountain rock, a symbol of alpine courage, sung about in The Sound of Music."],elderflower:["Fresh, sweet and green, a frothy hedgerow floral with muscat grape and lychee-like fruitiness.","Its creamy umbels are steeped into cordial and fizzy summer drinks, and its dark berries make syrup and wine."],rhododendron:["Fresh, green and lightly spicy, a cool mountain floral with a faint resinous, honeyed edge.","Big glossy evergreen shrubs with huge bloom trusses; some species make honey toxic enough to be called mad honey."],cotton:["Clean, soft and airy, like freshly laundered sheets with a powdery, slightly musky softness.","The plant behind T-shirts, denim and towels, its fluffy white bolls once picked by hand on vast plantations."],nasturtium:["Peppery, green and watercress-sharp, a spicy, slightly bitter floral with a fresh, mustardy bite.","Edible orange and red blooms scattered over salads, with round lily-pad foliage and seeds pickled like capers."],baobab:["Creamy, milky and slightly musky, an exotic night floral with a soft, sour-sweet tang.","A giant, bottle-trunked African tree that can live for thousands of years; its powdery pulp is sold as a superfood."],kewra:["Sweet, honeyed and green, a heady floral with a rich, slightly musky, hay-like depth.","Its distillate flavours biryanis, kebabs and milky desserts like rasmalai, from a spiky shrub on stilt-like props."],mignonette:["Green, earthy and violet-like, a delicate floral with a soft, spicy, slightly fruity freshness.","A modest, green-spiked plant prized by Victorians purely for its scent, once filling London window boxes."],cassie:["Warm, powdery and spicy, a violet-like floral with honeyed, leathery and anise-like depths.","A thorny shrub with fluffy yellow pompom blooms, a close cousin of mimosa, growing wild in warm dry regions."],camellia:["Soft, green and barely there, a delicate, tea-like floral with a dewy, slightly powdery freshness.","Coco Chanel’s favourite bloom, and close kin of the plant whose leaves make tea."],zdravetz:["Dry, green and herbal, a woody, faintly rose-like freshness with a resinous, almost tobacco-like edge.","A low, spreading cranesbill grown as tough garden ground cover, traditionally used as a charm for health and luck."],pittosporum:["Creamy, honeyed and spring-like, a waxy floral like neroli and jasmine on a summer evening.","A tough, glossy evergreen hedge of seaside gardens with clusters of creamy starry blooms in late spring."],plumblossom:["Delicate, almondy and fresh, a pale floral with a faint fruity, honeyed and powdery sweetness.","The first tree to bloom in late winter, one of the Four Gentlemen of Chinese painting, its sour fruit pickled."],sunflower:["Warm, sunny and pollen-dusted, a dry, slightly nutty green floral with a sunlit, grassy feel.","Its seeds become snacks and cooking oil; Van Gogh painted it repeatedly, and young heads track the sun."],daphne:["Lemony, spicy and intensely heady, a clove-tinged floral that fills a cold garden with sweetness.","A small, highly poisonous shrub whose tiny pink clusters scent gardens in the dead of the cold season."],passionflower:["Exotic, juicy and green, a tropical floral with a tart, fruity edge.","Intricate purple blooms whose parts missionaries read as symbols of the Crucifixion; a relative gives a tropical fruit."],amaryllis:["Soft, green and faintly sweet, a clean, gentle floral with a powdery, slightly spicy freshness.","Its name is popularly given to giant Christmas bulbs, though the true plant blooms on bare stems in late summer."],rangooncreeper:["Sweet, fruity and almondy, a heady tropical floral that deepens from fresh to rich as night falls.","A tropical climber whose dangling tubular blooms change from white to pink to red as they age."],tobaccoflower:["Heady and honeyed, a soft white floral that opens at dusk, with a green, slightly spicy sweetness.","Long tubular white blooms that open in the evening for moths, from a cousin of the cigarette leaf plant."],aldehydes:["Fizzy, waxy and soapy, like champagne bubbles and a hot iron on clean linen, adding sparkle and lift.","Lab-made fatty molecules famously overdosed in Chanel No. 5, also found in traces in coriander and orange peel."],hedione:["Airy, luminous and transparent, a citrusy jasmine-like glow that adds radiance and space more than a distinct smell.","A lab-made molecule modelled on a compound in jasmine, first used famously in Dior’s Eau Sauvage in 1966."],appleblossom:["Light, dewy and softly sweet, a pink-white spring freshness with a faint crisp fruitiness.","The pink-flushed spring blooms of the orchard tree that later gives us cider, crumbles and toffee-dipped fairground treats."],peachblossom:["Soft, sweet and powdery, a gentle pink floral with a faint velvety fruit-skin warmth.","A classical fable tells of a fisherman finding a hidden paradise by following a stream lined with these pink trees."],pearblossom:["Fresh, delicate and slightly green, a cool white floral like a spring breeze through an orchard.","Old poets compared its clouds of white spring bloom to snow, on the tree whose fruit is fermented into perry."],lemonblossom:["Waxy and bright, a white floral sparkling with zesty peel and a cool green edge.","The fragrant white buds that open on the evergreen whose sour yellow fruit gets squeezed over pancakes on Shrove Tuesday."],bellflower:["Airy, dewy and faintly green, a cool watery floral with a soft powdery hush.","A dainty wild plant of dry heaths and dunes, nodding papery violet cups on wiry stems in late summer."],bluebell:["Cool, green and sappy, a dewy hyacinth-like floral with a crisp woodland freshness.","Its nodding violet bells carpet ancient beech woods each spring, and digging up its wild bulbs is against the law."],wallflower:["Warm and velvety, a honeyed floral laced with spicy clove and a faint powdery sweetness.","A cottage-garden spring bedding plant with velvety rust and gold petals, and a word for someone shy at a dance."],goldenrod:["Honeyed and herbal, a warm hay-like floral with a resinous, slightly piney green bite.","Tall yellow plumes of late-summer roadsides, wrongly blamed for hay fever; Edison experimented with it as a rubber source."],babysbreath:["Airy, clean and powdery, a soft cloud of hazy white musk with a faint fresh sweetness.","The froth of tiny white sprays that florists tuck around roses in bouquets and bridal posies."],callalily:["Cool, watery and waxy, a clean green-white floral with a smooth, almost soapy elegance.","An elegant white funnel-shaped bloom carried in wedding bouquets and painted again and again by Georgia O'Keeffe."],poppy:["Soft, powdery and faintly green, a delicate airy floral with a hazy, dreamy calm.","The scarlet bloom worn in paper form each November to remember the war dead."],kowhai:["Honeyed and gentle, a sunny floral with a soft, slightly woody warmth.","A small tree hung with drooping, beak-shaped yellow blooms in spring that nectar-feeding birds flock to."],galbanum:["Piercingly green and bitter, like snapped stems and green pepper over a resinous, balsamic base.","A milky gum resin from a giant fennel relative, named in Exodus among the ingredients of the holy incense."],mint:["Cool, sharp and mentholated, a sweet green chill that feels like a frosty breath.","The cooling flavour of toothpaste, chewing gum, humbugs and after-dinner chocolate thins."],sage:["Musky, herbal and slightly boozy, with warm hay, tea and a soft ambery depth.","A tall herb once used to clear grit from the eyes, and to give German wines a muscat flavour."],rosemary:["Crisp, resinous and camphorous, a piney herb with a bright, clean, sunlit sharpness.","The needle-leaved herb pushed into roast lamb, which Ophelia offers in Hamlet as the plant for remembrance."],basil:["Green, peppery and anise-sweet, with a warm clove-like spice and a fresh sappy snap.","The herb pounded with pine nuts, garlic and Parmesan into pesto, and torn over a margherita pizza."],tea:["Dry, slightly smoky and tannic, a calm, bitter-fresh warmth like steam from a cup.","Second only to water as the world's most drunk beverage, brewed from the dried foliage of a shrub."],fig:["Milky, green and creamy, a sappy freshness with a coconut-tinged, soft and slightly nutty sweetness.","Adam and Eve sewed its broad foliage into aprons, and its seedy sticky fruit fills a classic biscuit roll."],eucalyptus:["Cool, camphorous and medicinal, a clean sinus-clearing blast of minty freshness.","The gum tree that koalas feed on, and the vapour in chest rubs, inhalers and cough sweets."],thyme:["Warm, dry and medicinal, a phenolic herb like a sunbaked hillside of scrub.","Listed fourth in the Scarborough Fair refrain, it goes into bouquet garni and gives mouthwash its antiseptic bite."],lemongrass:["Sharp, sherbet-bright citrus with a fresh, slightly gingery and earthy bite.","The fibrous stalk bruised into Thai green curry paste and hot and sour tom yum soup."],davana:["Fruity and boozy, like dried apricot soaked in brandy, with a hay-like herbal warmth.","A small silvery herb offered to Shiva in Hindu temples and woven into garlands."],artemisia:["Bitter, dry and camphorous, a silvery green aroma with an aromatic, slightly medicinal edge.","The bitter grey-leaved plant behind absinthe, whose German name gave vermouth its own name."],angelica:["Musky, peppery and green, with an earthy, celery-like depth and a faint sweetness.","Its candied stems decorate trifles and cakes, and it is a key botanical in gin and Chartreuse."],myrtle:["Fresh, camphorous and softly spicy, a clean green aroma gentler than eucalyptus.","An evergreen sacred to Venus; sprigs go in royal wedding bouquets and its berries make a Sardinian liqueur."],verbena:["Bright, sherbet-like citrus with a soft green sweetness, light and effortlessly refreshing.","A favourite after-dinner tisane in French cafés, brewed from a shrub's sharply citrus-scented foliage."],olive:["Green, slightly bitter and fruity, with a dry, oily, sun-warmed woody softness.","The dove brought Noah a sprig of it as a sign of peace, and its fruit is pressed for salad oil."],carrotseed:["Earthy and woody, like a freshly pulled vegetable, with a faint violet and musky warmth.","Its wild form is Queen Anne's lace, whose lacy white umbels hide a single dark red floret at the centre."],mate:["Hay-like and green, with a smoky, tobacco-tinged dryness and a bitter tea warmth.","A caffeinated infusion sipped through a metal straw from a hollow gourd and passed round among friends."],buchu:["Intensely fruity and sulphurous, like crushed blackcurrant with a sharp minty, medicinal tang.","A small aromatic shrub once sold by Victorian chemists as a urinary remedy, and steeped in brandy as a tonic."],rhubarb:["Tart, crisp and green, a sour-fruity zing with a juicy, slightly earthy snap.","Its sour pink sticks are baked into crumbles with custard, often forced in dark sheds, and its foliage is poisonous."],tarragon:["Green and anise-sweet, a liquorice-tinged herb with a fresh, peppery bite.","The herb that flavours béarnaise sauce, steeped in French vinegar and counted among the fines herbes."],oregano:["Warm, pungent and peppery, a dry, sun-scorched herb with a medicinal, phenolic bite.","The dried herb shaken over pizza and Greek salads, a cousin of marjoram."],calamus:["Warm and spicy, a bitter leathery green with hints of cinnamon and damp reeds.","A reed-like marsh plant with iris-like foliage, once candied as a confection and used in bitters and absinthe."],hay:["Warm, dry and sweetish, a sun-dried coumarin glow tinged with tobacco and honey.","Dried forage stacked in barns for winter animal feed, seen as rolled bales dotting late-summer fields."],bamboo:["Watery, green and airy, a clean, slightly woody freshness like a breeze through tall canes.","The fast-growing giant grass that pandas chew, whose hollow canes make fishing rods and scaffolding."],cannabis:["Green, resinous and peppery, with a skunky, herbal edge and a slightly sweet warmth.","A plant grown for rope fibre and seed oil, notorious for the psychoactive buds people smoke."],rooibos:["Warm, honeyed and nutty, a soft woody infusion with a faint smoky sweetness.","A caffeine-free brew that pours a fox-red cup, the favourite drink of Mma Ramotswe in Alexander McCall Smith's novels."],teatree:["Sharp, medicinal and camphorous, a spicy antiseptic freshness like a first-aid cabinet.","The antiseptic oil dabbed on spots and added to acne washes and dandruff shampoos."],lemonmyrtle:["Intensely bright, sherbet-like citrus with a creamy, candy-sweet softness and a herbal edge.","A rainforest tree with one of the highest citral contents of any plant, used as bush food in shortbread."],labradortea:["Resinous and balsamic, a camphor-tinged spicy freshness with a faint fruity warmth.","A bog shrub of the far north with rusty-felted undersides to its foliage, brewed by Indigenous peoples."],oolong:["Roasted and creamy, a toasty infusion with soft floral and stone-fruit notes.","A partly oxidised brew between green and black, rolled into tight balls and poured gongfu-style into tiny cups."],manuka:["Warm, herbal and medicinal, with a spicy, resinous sweetness and a faint antiseptic tang.","Bees foraging its blossom make a pricey antibacterial spread, graded by a UMF rating on the jar."],hops:["Bitter, green and herbal, with a spicy, slightly cheesy edge and a drowsy calm.","The papery green flowers that give beer its bitter bite, also stuffed into pillows to aid sleep."],paramela:["Resinous and herbal, a sticky balsamic freshness with a soft, slightly fruity sweetness.","A small, sticky, resin-coated shrub of the windswept Patagonian steppe, used in local folk remedies."],creosote:["Smoky, tarry and resinous, like hot desert air the moment a thunderstorm breaks.","A tough desert shrub that gives the desert its famous smell of rain, with one clonal ring thousands of years old."],gentian:["Bitter, earthy and dry, with a faint honeyed sweetness under a woody, medicinal depth.","A bitter mountain plant that flavours Angostura bitters and the French aperitif Suze."],matcha:["Creamy, vegetal and slightly bitter, a smooth umami freshness like steamed spinach and cut hay.","Whisked into a frothy jade bowl in a formal ceremony, and now blended into lattes, ice cream and chocolate bars."],ginseng:["Earthy, bitter and slightly sweet, a dry, woody warmth with a faint medicinal edge.","A forked, man-shaped tonic prized in Eastern medicine for vitality and added to energy drinks."],niaouli:["Camphorous and clean, a cool eucalyptus-like freshness with a soft, slightly sweet edge.","Oil of a paperbark tree, close cousin of the spot-treatment oil, once sold as the antiseptic Gomenol."],lichen:["Cool, damp and mineral, a bitter, earthy freshness like a stone wall after rain.","A leathery fungus and alga partnership of the tundra, once boiled into famine bread and still sold as throat pastilles."],fennel:["Warm, anise-like and liquorice-sugared, with a soft green, slightly peppery freshness.","Sugar-coated and chewed after curries as a breath freshener, it also flavours Italian sausage and absinthe."],shiso:["Spicy and minty, with a cumin and cinnamon warmth over a sharp citrus snap.","A serrated herb served beside sashimi; its purple form dyes pickled ume plums a deep red."],palmarosa:["Soft and floral, a geranium-like sweetness over a dry, faintly hay-like and citrus edge.","Its oil was long used to stretch the costliest floral attar, and was once traded as 'Turkish geranium oil'."],citronella:["Sharp, lemony and fresh, a bright citrus with a dry, slightly woody, hay-like bite.","The smell of mosquito-repelling candles and garden torches on summer evenings."],tomatoleaf:["Pungent, green and sappy, a bitter, earthy freshness that clings to your fingers.","The sharp smell left on your hands after pinching out side shoots of a staked salad crop on an allotment."],khella:["Warm and herbal, with a dry spicy edge and a faintly sweet, green earthiness.","Its stiff dried umbel rays were used as tooth-cleaning sticks, and its compound inspired the asthma drug cromolyn."],cucumber:["Cool, watery and crisp, a clean, melon-like freshness like a chilled slice on the skin.","Sliced over tired eyes at spas, and into Pimm's and dainty sandwiches at afternoon tea."],cactus:["Watery, green and juicy, a cool, light freshness like sap from a cut succulent.","A spiny desert succulent whose paddles are grilled as a vegetable and which hosts the cochineal insect."],laurel:["Aromatic and spicy, a camphorous herb with a clove-like warmth and dry green freshness.","Its wreath crowned Greek victors and poets, and a dried one goes into stews and bouquet garni."],mitti:["Cool, mineral and dusty, like the first monsoon rain striking parched, sun-scorched ground.","Captures the scent of first rain on dry ground, a smell two Australian scientists gave a name in 1964."],grass:["Sharp, sappy and dewy, like a summer lawn just after the mower has passed.","The smell of a Saturday lawn after the mower, released by wounded plants as a chemical distress signal."],ivy:["Dark, bitter-green and shaded, a cool damp freshness with a faintly peppery, earthy edge.","An evergreen climber cloaking old walls and tree trunks, partnered with holly in a Christmas carol."],bluetansy:["Fruity, herbal and camphorous, a soft apple-like freshness over a cool, medicinal edge.","Its oil is a startling deep indigo, coloured by chamazulene, and is popular in face oils and serums."],marjoram:["Warm, soft and herbal, a gentle woody spice, rounder and milder than oregano.","The gentler cousin of oregano, used in German sausages and liver pâté and sprinkled on potatoes."],hyssop:["Camphorous and herbal, warm and slightly honeyed, with a bitter, medicinal sharpness.","A Biblical purifying herb, 'purge me with it' in Psalm 51, and a botanical in absinthe and Chartreuse."],melissa:["Soft, green and citrus-fresh, a gentle honeyed herb with a calm, sunny lightness.","Its Greek name means honeybee, and Carmelite nuns distilled it into a famous cordial water for nerves."],wintergreen:["Sharp, minty-sweet and medicinal, a cooling blast like root beer and sports rub.","The cooling medicinal scent of muscle-rub creams like Deep Heat, and a classic flavour in root beer."],sweetgrass:["Warm and hay-like, a soft coumarin glow with almond and creamy, toasty depth.","A single blade is steeped in every bottle of a famous flavoured vodka, and braids are burnt in Native American ceremonies."],lovage:["Savoury, celery-like and yeasty, a warm herbal depth like a simmering stock pot.","Called the Maggi herb in Germany for its stock-cube smell, a tall celery-flavoured herb of cottage gardens."],cajeput:["Camphorous, fresh and medicinal, a sharp eucalyptus-like coolness with a faint fruity warmth.","Paperbark oil found in Southeast Asian households in small bottles, rubbed on chests and tummies for colds and colic."],ravintsara:["Cool, clean and eucalyptus-like, a clear airy freshness with a faint spicy warmth.","Comes from the same species that yields mothball-like crystals, yet this type is rich in eucalyptus's main molecule."],pandan:["Nutty, milky and warm, like freshly cooked basmati rice with a soft green sweetness.","The long blades that tint Southeast Asian chiffon cakes and kaya jam bright green and flavour coconut rice."],yarrow:["Herbal and camphorous, bitter-green with a faint sweet, slightly medicinal warmth.","A feathery wayside plant with flat white heads, used to staunch battlefield wounds and to cast the I Ching."],clover:["Honeyed, soft and hay-like, a gentle floral freshness like a summer lawn in bloom.","A four-lobed one is said to bring luck, and its round heads feed honeybees across lawns and pastures."],cedarleaf:["Sharp, camphorous and green, a herbal-woody freshness with a slightly sour, medicinal edge.","An evergreen hedging conifer whose foliage brew saved Jacques Cartier's scurvy-stricken crew in 1536."],witchhazel:["Mild, green and slightly sweet, a clean, astringent herbal freshness like a cool tonic.","The astringent toner on every chemist's shelf, dabbed on spots and bruises; its forked twigs were used for dowsing."],santolina:["Sharp, bitter and camphorous, a dry herbal aroma with a chamomile-like edge.","A silvery-grey dwarf shrub clipped into knot gardens, with button-like yellow blooms, used to repel moths."],fern:["Green, mossy and herbal, a cool forest-floor freshness with a hay-like, soapy sweetness.","These flowerless spore plants sparked a Victorian collecting mania and gave a classic barbershop perfume family its name."],dill:["Fresh and green, with a sweet caraway-anise note and a slightly sour, briny edge.","The feathery herb of pickled gherkins and Scandinavian gravlax."],beetroot:["Earthy, damp and mineral, with a sweet, slightly metallic depth like freshly dug soil.","The vegetable that turns borscht crimson and stains your fingers, often sold pickled in vinegar."],mushroom:["Earthy, damp and savoury, like a forest floor in autumn with a spicy, piney edge.","A prized autumn fungus pushing up under red pines, sold at astonishing prices and steamed in clear broth."],blackcurrant:["Tart, green and catty, a sharp sulphurous fruitiness with a jammy dark berry depth.","The fruit in a purple children's cordial and in the liqueur mixed with white wine to make a Kir."],pineapple:["Juicy, sharp and sweet-tart, a sunny tropical burst with a sugary, fizzy brightness.","The crowned tropical fruit topping the controversial ham pizza, and once a symbol of hospitality on gateposts."],apple:["Crisp, juicy and tart, a bright fruity snap like biting into a cold, fresh fruit.","The fruit said to have fallen on Newton's head, and Snow White's poisoned bite."],pear:["Juicy, watery and softly sweet, a crisp, cool fruit with a delicate dewy freshness.","Fermented into perry, and poached with chocolate sauce in the dessert Belle Hélène."],peach:["Velvety, juicy and creamy, a soft sweet fruit with a warm, fuzzy-skinned lushness.","Served over ice cream with raspberry sauce in Escoffier's Melba, and puréed with prosecco for a Bellini."],raspberry:["Tart-sweet and jammy, a bright red berry with a soft violet-tinged sweetness.","A soft red berry from canes in summer gardens, and the rude noise you blow with your tongue."],strawberry:["Jammy, sugary and slightly green, like crushed red summer berries with a candy-floss sweetness.","The red berry dipped in cream at Wimbledon, unusual for wearing its tiny seeds on the outside."],coconut:["Creamy, nutty-sweet and sun-warmed, like suntan lotion and a tropical cocktail on the beach.","A hairy brown shell you crack open for white flesh, found in piña coladas, Bounty bars and Thai curries."],plum:["Dark, jammy and winey, a ripe stone-fruit sweetness with a tart-skinned, faintly almond depth.","Victoria is the best-known British variety, a purple-red stone fruit for crumbles, jams and the sauce served with crispy duck."],cherry:["Sweet and almondy with a tart red-fruit juiciness, like a cocktail garnish or a cough sweet.","The glossy red fruit on a stalk, candied atop sundaes and Bakewell tarts, from the tree behind Japan's spring blossom festivals."],lychee:["Juicy, floral and sweetly watery, with a perfumed hint of rose and a faint tropical tartness.","A small fruit with bumpy red skin you peel to reveal translucent white flesh around a glossy brown stone."],passionfruit:["Tart, tropical and sharply exotic, a sulphurous-sweet juiciness that bursts like a fresh sorbet.","A wrinkled purple shell scooped out for its seedy golden pulp, spooned over pavlova and shaken into cocktails."],blackberry:["Dark, juicy and slightly tart, a hedgerow-jam sweetness with a green, leafy edge.","The thorny hedgerow fruit picked in late summer for crumbles, classically paired with apple."],mango:["Lush, juicy and resinous, a ripe tropical sweetness with a faintly piney, sappy bite.","A tropical fruit blended into lassi, with sunny orange flesh clinging to a large, flat, fibrous stone."],apricot:["Velvety, sunny and gently sweet, a soft stone-fruit note with a suede-like, peachy fuzz.","A small orange stone fruit, often dried into chewy halves, and the jam spread inside a Viennese Sachertorte."],melon:["Cool, watery and sweet, a fresh green juiciness that evokes the aquatic fragrances of the 1990s.","Pale green or orange flesh scooped from a netted or smooth rind, often served wrapped in Parma ham."],pomegranate:["Tart, ruby-bright and slightly tannic, a crisp juicy sharpness with a dry, astringent finish.","A leathery red globe packed with jewel-like seeds, the fruit Persephone ate in the underworld in Greek myth."],persimmon:["Honeyed and mellow, a soft orange-fleshed sweetness with a faintly apricot, slightly astringent edge.","A glossy orange autumn fruit shaped like a tomato, mouth-puckering when unripe and often hung up to dry."],papaya:["Soft, musky and buttery-tropical, a mellow sweetness with a faintly cheesy, overripe richness.","A pear-shaped tropical fruit with orange flesh around a cavity of black seeds, its enzyme used to tenderise meat."],kiwi:["Tangy, green and juicy, a crisp sweet-sour freshness with a cool, slightly watery edge.","A fuzzy brown egg-shaped fruit, cut open to show bright green flesh ringed with tiny black seeds."],quince:["Honeyed, floral and appley-pear, a fragrant yellow fruitiness with a faintly waxy, musky peel.","A hard, fuzzy yellow fruit too tough to eat raw, turning pink when slow-cooked into a firm paste eaten with Manchego."],sapodilla:["Soft, malty and milky-sweet, like brown sugar, ripe pear and a hint of caramel cream.","Its tree's latex, chicle, was the original base of chewing gum, and its brown fruit tastes of brown sugar."],seabuckthorn:["Sharp, tangy and sunny, a fiercely sour orange tartness hinting at pineapple and citrus.","Tiny, fiercely sour orange fruits crowded on a thorny, silver-leaved shrub, pressed into juices and skincare oils."],cloudberry:["Juicy, tart and honeyed, a bright amber fruitiness recalling apricot and sharp apple.","An amber, raspberry-shaped fruit growing one per stem in Arctic bogs, so prized that picking it is regulated by law."],lingonberry:["Tart, bright and slightly bitter, a crisp red-fruit sourness with a cool woodland freshness.","A tart little red forest fruit, its jam served alongside meatballs, mashed potato and creamy gravy."],mulberry:["Dark, jammy and gently tart, a deep purple-fruit sweetness with a soft, slightly earthy edge.","Its leaves are the only food of silkworms, and its fruit stains fingers purple; children go round its bush in a nursery rhyme."],cherimoya:["Creamy and tropical, a soft, milky sweetness blending banana, papaya and ripe pear.","A scaly, heart-shaped green fruit with spoonable white flesh and shiny black seeds, best eaten chilled."],rosehip:["Tart, tangy and slightly earthy, a dried red-fruit sharpness with a herbal, tea-like warmth.","The red berry-like fruits left on wild briars after flowering, made into vitamin C syrup in wartime Britain and herbal teas."],guava:["Musky, tropical and sweetly pungent, a ripe coral-fleshed juiciness with a green, faintly sulphurous rind.","A round tropical fruit full of hard seeds, boiled into a sweet paste and baked into Cuban pastries."],watermelon:["Cool, crisp and lightly sweet, like biting into chilled red flesh on a hot summer's day.","A huge striped green fruit with juicy red flesh and black seeds, sliced into wedges at picnics."],marula:["Tart, juicy and creamy, a tropical sweetness hinting at mango, citrus and soft fermentation.","Its plum-sized yellow drupes flavour a South African cream liqueur with an elephant on the label."],dragonfruit:["Light, watery and gently sweet, a delicate tropical note somewhere between kiwi and melon.","Shocking pink and green-scaled outside, it grows on a climbing cactus and hides white flesh speckled with tiny black seeds."],banana:["Creamy, sweet and slightly boozy, like a ripe yellow peel with a hint of pear-drop candy.","A curved yellow fruit, the classic potassium-rich snack, whose discarded skin is the slapstick slipping hazard."],blueberry:["Soft, inky and jammy, a dusky purple-fruit sweetness with a gentle tartness.","Small, dusky purple fruits with a powdery bloom, baked into American muffins and pancakes and hailed as a superfood."],acai:["Dark and earthy-sweet, a purple fruitiness with hints of grape, cocoa and a creamy texture.","The pulp of an Amazon palm fruit, served frozen as a purple smoothie bowl topped with granola and banana."],feijoa:["Green, tangy and tropical, a creamy fruitiness with a cool minty lift and faint floral sweetness.","An egg-shaped green fruit loved in New Zealand back gardens, halved and scooped out with a teaspoon in autumn."],nectarine:["Juicy, bright and sweet, a smooth-skinned stone-fruit freshness with a tangy, slightly floral bite.","Essentially a peach without the fuzz, a single gene giving it smooth, glossy red-blushed skin."],cranberry:["Sharp, tart and bright, a crisp red-fruit sourness with a slightly bitter, dry edge.","Harvested by flooding bogs so the floating red fruits can be skimmed off, then made into sauce for Christmas turkey."],gooseberry:["Tart and catty, a sharp juicy sourness with a sulphurous tang, like a crisp Sauvignon Blanc.","Hairy, veined little fruits from a thorny bush, cooked and folded into cream for a classic summer fool."],redcurrant:["Bright, tart and glassy, a sharp red-berry sourness with a fresh, slightly green tang.","Tiny translucent scarlet fruits hanging in strings, set into a jelly served with roast lamb."],grape:["Sweet, juicy and slightly foxy, like purple soda or a glass of just-pressed juice.","Grown on vines in bunches and crushed for wine, or dried into raisins and sultanas."],pinkpepper:["Bright, rosy and lightly spicy, a sparkling resinous tingle with a sweet, berry-like fizz.","Papery reddish berries from a tree related to the cashew, sold in colourful mixed grinders though unrelated to the table spice they resemble."],pepper:["Dry, crackling and warm, a sharp spicy bite with a fresh, faintly woody, resinous lift.","Ground fresh from a mill onto almost every Western dinner plate, the partner of salt in the cruet set."],cardamom:["Cool, eucalyptus-fresh and sweetly spicy, with a camphorous lift and a warm, resinous softness.","Little green papery pods that flavour masala chai, Scandinavian sweet buns and Arabic coffee."],cinnamon:["Warm, sweet and woody-spicy, like a cosy bakery on a winter morning.","The sweet spice dusted on cappuccino, swirled through Swedish buns and stirred as a stick into mulled wine."],clove:["Hot, medicinal and spicy-sweet, a numbing warmth that recalls an old-fashioned dentist's surgery.","Nail-shaped spice pressed into oranges for Christmas pomanders, studded into glazed ham, and dabbed on aching teeth."],nutmeg:["Warm, woody and sweetly spicy, with a soft, slightly fiery, eggnog-like cosiness.","A brown oval kernel grated over custard tarts and eggnog, once so valuable that colonial powers fought over its islands."],saffron:["Leathery, honeyed and metallic, a dry, hay-like warmth with a faint bitter-sweet glow.","Crimson threads worth more than their weight in gold, turning paella and risotto alla milanese a deep yellow."],ginger:["Zesty, warm and peppery, a fizzy, lemony spice with a fresh, sparkling heat.","The knobbly spice in stir-fries, dunking biscuits and fizzy beer, served pink and pickled beside sushi."],coriander:["Spicy, sweet and slightly citrusy, with a soft warm woodiness and a hint of lavender.","Its leaves split diners into lovers and those who taste soap, while its round dried fruits flavour curries and gin."],cumin:["Warm, earthy and sweaty-spicy, a dry toasted note with a faintly animalic, skin-like edge.","The earthy, smoky spice of chilli con carne, falafel and dal, often sizzled whole in hot oil."],staranise:["Sweet, warm and liquorice-like, a smooth, cool spice with a faintly woody, balsamic softness.","Eight-pointed woody pods that flavour Chinese five-spice and pho broth, and once supplied the raw material for Tamiflu."],sichuan:["Zesty, lemony and electric, a tingling citrus-floral spark with a fresh, green spiciness.","The husks behind mala, the numbing, lip-tingling buzz of hotpot and kung pao chicken."],pimento:["Warm and spicy-sweet, blending clove, cinnamon and nutmeg into one rounded, peppery glow.","Dried brown berries from a Caribbean tree, essential to jerk seasoning and named for tasting of several spices at once."],bay:["Spicy, clove-like and warm, a fresh herbal note with a rum-tinged, old barbershop edge.","Its oil was steeped in rum to make the classic Caribbean aftershave splashed on in old-fashioned barbershops."],caraway:["Warm, sharp and slightly minty, like the spicy, dill-like tang of a dark rye loaf.","Little crescent-shaped spice flecking rye bread, old-fashioned British seed cake and the Nordic spirit aquavit."],turmeric:["Earthy, warm and slightly woody, with a dry, peppery, ginger-like bitterness.","The bright yellow-orange spice that colours curries and golden milk lattes, and stains everything it touches."],celeryseed:["Green, savoury and warm, a strong vegetal spice like a bubbling pot of vegetable stock.","Its crunchy stalks garnish a Bloody Mary and join onion and carrot as the base of countless soups."],grainsofparadise:["Hot, citrusy and resinous, a bright, prickly warmth with a soft, cardamom-like woody hum.","A West African spice from a ginger relative, prized in medieval Europe and used today to flavour some gins."],mace:["Warm, sweet and spicy, a softer, more refined cousin of nutmeg with a gentle citrus lift.","Dried into orange blades, it seasons British potted shrimps and comes from the very same tree as nutmeg."],molle:["Rosy, resinous and gently hot, a bright, slightly citrus spice with a sweet, sparkling lift.","A weeping evergreen whose rosy berries the ancient Wari brewed into chicha, now planted as a street tree worldwide."],paprika:["Warm, mellow and earthy, a dry red spice like roasted red peppers with a faint smokiness.","The red powder that colours goulash and chorizo, and is dusted over devilled eggs."],fenugreek:["Nutty, savoury and caramel-like, with a maple syrup sweetness and a warm curry-house depth.","Its hard little yellow kernels flavour curries and imitation maple syrup, and eating them can make sweat smell sweet."],galangal:["Sharp, peppery and camphorous, a piney, citrusy spice with a fresh, earthy bite.","Woody slices of it float in tom yum and tom kha soups, a firmer, piney cousin of a common stir-fry spice."],cassia:["Hot, sweet and fiery, a sharper, more pungent take on a classic baking spice.","Thick, rough quills that American supermarkets sell under a more famous spice's name, and a staple of five-spice powder."],cubeb:["Hot, woody and camphorous, a dry spice with a cool, eucalyptus-like freshness.","Small spice berries with a little stalk attached, once smoked in medicinal cigarettes and now found in some gins."],asafoetida:["Pungent, sulphurous and garlicky, a powerful oniony stench that mellows into a savoury, leek-like warmth.","A dried gum from giant fennel, nicknamed devil's dung, used in Indian dal as a stand-in for onion and garlic."],wasabi:["Sharp, green and nose-tingling, a cool, watery heat with a fresh, horseradish-like bite.","The green paste served with sushi, usually imitated outside its homeland with dyed horseradish and mustard."],blackcardamom:["Smoky, camphorous and resinous, a campfire-dried spice with a cool, menthol edge.","Big, wrinkled pods dried over open fires, dropped whole into biryanis and ground into garam masala."],nigella:["Peppery, smoky and herbaceous, a dry toasted spice with an oregano-like, slightly bitter edge.","Tiny inky teardrops scattered over naan and Turkish breads, from a close relative of the garden flower love-in-a-mist."],timut:["Zingy grapefruit and passion-fruit brightness over a tingling, woody spice, sparkling and fresh.","A prickly ash berry that makes the tongue tingle, a close cousin of the numbing spice in Chinese hotpot."],sandalwood:["Creamy, milky and smooth, a soft, warm woodiness like polished temple timber.","Carved into fans and prayer beads, and ground into a paste for forehead marks in Hindu worship."],cedar:["Dry, clean and sharp as pencil shavings, a crisp, slightly resinous woodiness.","The aromatic timber lining chests and wardrobes to keep moths away, and the smell of freshly sharpened pencils."],vetiver:["Earthy, smoky and green, like damp soil and dry grass with a bitter, nutty smokiness.","A tall tropical grass planted to hold soil against erosion, woven into window screens that are wetted to cool Indian homes."],patchouli:["Earthy, dark and damp, like a forest floor or old cellar, with a sweet, cocoa-like richness.","The signature scent of 1960s hippies, once packed with Indian shawls to keep moths away on long voyages."],oud:["Dark, smoky and medicinal, a resinous, animalic woodiness with a leathery, barnyard depth.","Resin-darkened heartwood formed when a tropical tree fights fungal infection, burned as incense across the Middle East."],guaiac:["Smoky and tarry, a warm campfire note softened by a faint, sweet hint of rose.","A very hard, dense South American timber whose sawdust yields an oil so thick it is nearly solid at room temperature."],birch:["Smoky and tarry, like a well-worn saddle, polished boots and the ash of a woodstove.","A white-barked tree whose tar once tanned hides, and whose sap is tapped in spring for a refreshing drink."],cypress:["Green, resinous and dry, a crisp evergreen freshness with a slightly smoky, herbal woodiness.","Tall, flame-shaped dark trees lining Tuscan roads and Mediterranean cemeteries, long a symbol of mourning."],oakmoss:["Damp, inky and earthy, like a shady forest floor with a salty, leathery bitterness.","A grey-green lichen that grows on tree branches, the backbone of classic chypre perfumes."],juniper:["Crisp, resinous and bracing, a piney, peppery freshness with a cool, slightly bittersweet bite.","Its dusky blue cones, often mistaken for fruits, give the defining flavour to the spirit in a classic G and T."],hinoki:["Clean, lemony and resinous, like freshly planed pale timber in a steamy bathhouse.","A sacred cypress whose pale timber builds temples and shrines and makes deep, fragrant soaking tubs."],palosanto:["Sweet, smoky and minty-citrus, like a smouldering stick of incense with a bright lemon-peel lift.","Sticks from fallen trees are lit and smudged like sage for cleansing smoke in wellness and yoga circles."],rosewood:["Soft, floral and woody, a gentle sweet-spicy freshness with a lightly peppery, lavender-like note.","An endangered Amazonian tree once felled for its linalool-rich oil, now protected by international trade rules."],fir:["Fresh, cold and sappy, like a snowy evergreen forest and a just-cut Christmas tree.","A classic Christmas tree whose clear sap, gathered from bark blisters, was once used to mount microscope slides."],oak:["Dry, toasted and warm, with a mellow coconut and vanilla smoothness like an old barrel.","The timber of the barrels that age wine, whisky and cognac, lending them toasted, vanilla-like notes."],cade:["Smoky, tarry and phenolic, like a dying campfire, smoked fish and old leather.","A dark tar from a prickly Mediterranean juniper, long used in ointments for skin conditions and on livestock."],spikenard:["Earthy, musty and animalic, a dark, damp woodiness with a sweet, valerian-like heaviness.","The costly ointment Mary poured over Jesus's feet in the Gospels, prized since antiquity."],cascarilla:["Warm, peppery and nutmeg-like, a spicy, slightly smoky woodiness with a faint bitter edge.","A small Caribbean shrub that flavours Campari and other bitters, once also added to tobacco for its scent."],amyris:["Soft, balmy and gently woody, a mellow, slightly sweet smoothness with a faint oily depth.","A scrubby Caribbean tree long sold as West Indian sandalwood, though it is no relation at all."],costus:["Animalic and furry, like wet dog, unwashed hair and old leather softened by powdery orris.","A tall mountain plant of the daisy family, traded across ancient Asia as medicine and incense, and now endangered."],cypriol:["Smoky, earthy and leathery, a dark, dry woodiness with an oud-like, slightly animal edge.","A damp-loving sedge related to the reed Egyptians pressed into writing sheets, and the source of that reed's note in perfume."],teak:["Dry, smooth and slightly leathery, a warm, clean timber note with a hint of oil.","The golden timber of yacht decks and garden benches, naturally oily and resistant to weather and rot."],mahogany:["Warm, smooth and slightly ambery, like polished reddish furniture in an old library.","The rich reddish-brown timber of Chippendale furniture and fine cabinets, heavily logged in colonial Central America."],okoume:["Soft, dry and lightly resinous, a pale timber note with a faint peppery, elemi-like brightness.","A tall rainforest tree peeled into thin, lightweight veneers for boat-building panels and furniture."],buddhawood:["Smoky, leathery and earthy, a dark dry timber note with a vetiver-like depth and faint sweetness.","A small tree of dry inland scrubland whose dense, oily, termite-proof timber was long prized for fence posts."],bluecypress:["Smoky-sweet and dry, a soft timber note with a faint fruity lift and a calm, quiet glow.","A conifer of tropical savannas whose distilled oil comes out unusually tinted azure by the compound guaiazulene."],vanuatusandal:["Creamy, milky and soft, a smooth sweet timber that melts warmly into the skin.","Nineteenth-century traders stripped whole islands of these fragrant trees to sell in China for incense and carving."],massoia:["Milky and creamy, like coconut milk poured over warm, sweet, faintly spicy timber.","A tropical rainforest tree whose coconut-scented oil is also used as a food flavouring and a traditional remedy."],priprioca:["Earthy and woody with a peppery edge, like a softer, greener vetiver dug from damp soil.","An Amazonian sedge sold in market bundles for a perfumed bath taken for luck at festivals and New Year."],cork:["Dry, dusty and faintly smoky, like sniffing the stopper drawn from an old wine bottle.","Stripped by hand from living oaks every nine years or so, it seals wine bottles and lines noticeboards."],siberianfir:["Cold, clean and green, like a snowy conifer forest with a soft balsamic sweetness.","A hardy evergreen of the frozen taiga forests that can survive winter frosts of around minus fifty degrees."],ebony:["Dark, dry and smoky, a polished black timber note with a cool, austere depth.","The jet-black, dense timber traditionally used for the sharps of a piano and the fingerboards of violins."],araucaria:["Resinous and dry, a sharp conifer timber note with a clean, slightly sappy edge.","A spiky, prehistoric-looking conifer of Victorian gardens, nicknamed because climbing its branches would baffle any primate."],thanaka:["Soft, powdery and creamy, a pale milky timber note like cool paste drying on skin.","Ground with water on a flat stone, it is worn in yellowish patterns on the cheeks as everyday sunscreen and make-up."],iliahi:["Soft, creamy and milky, a sweet smooth timber with a slightly drier, cleaner edge.","Early nineteenth-century chiefs dug ship-shaped pits to measure loads of this fragrant tree for the China trade."],kanuka:["Fresh, piney and gently spicy, a bright green lift like crushed foliage of a hillside shrub.","A close cousin of manuka, this tea-tree shrub colonises cleared hillsides and also gives bees a pale honey."],spruce:["Fresh, cold and resinous, like crushing a sprig of conifer in a winter forest.","A boreal evergreen whose tips were brewed into a beer by sailors and settlers to ward off scurvy."],camphor:["Sharp, cool and medicinal, a piercing clean blast that clears the nose like menthol.","Its crystals give chest rubs and old-fashioned mothballs their cooling, medicinal smell."],cabreuva:["Softly floral and balsamic over timber, gentle and sweet like dried flowers kept in a cedar box.","A slow-growing Atlantic Forest tree whose oil is a major natural source of the floral molecule nerolidol."],redwood:["Dry, softly sweet timber wrapped in cool, damp, mossy forest air after the fog rolls in.","The world's tallest living trees, some two thousand years old, which draw much of their summer water from fog."],deodar:["Dry, firm and faintly sweet, like pencil shavings with a soft, warm resinous glow.","A towering mountain conifer whose name derives from Sanskrit words meaning timber of the gods."],isoesuper:["Smooth, dry and velvety, a radiant transparent glow of timber and amber that hovers around the skin.","A lab-made molecule from 1973, so subtle some people barely smell it; one cult fragrance contains almost nothing else."],cashmeran:["Soft, musky and cosy with spicy, piney facets, like burying your nose in a plush knitted jumper.","A lab-made molecule from the late 1960s, named after luxurious goat-hair knitwear, which occurs nowhere in nature."],frankincense:["Lemony, peppery and cool, like smoke curling through a stone church during mass.","One of the three gifts the Magi brought to the infant Jesus, alongside gold and a bitter embalming gum."],myrrh:["Bitter, balsamic and medicinal, a dusky resin with a dry, slightly mushroomy warmth.","One of the three gifts of the Magi, used by ancient Egyptians for embalming and still found in some mouthwashes."],labdanum:["Rich, sticky and leathery-sweet, a deep resinous warmth with a faintly animalic, honeyed glow.","In ancient Crete it was combed from the beards of goats that had brushed against rockrose shrubs."],benzoin:["Warm and sweet, like caramel, cinnamon and powdery vanilla melting together.","The key ingredient of Friar's Balsam, the old steam inhalation remedy, and a common ingredient of church incense."],elemi:["Bright, lemony and peppery, a fresh resin with a clean, faintly fennel-like sparkle.","A soft fragrant gum from tropical trees related to the pili nut, once used in varnishes and healing ointments."],styrax:["Dark and balsamic, smelling of leather, cinnamon and smoke with a sweet, slightly plasticky edge.","A thick, honey-like gum from an oriental sweetgum, cousin of the street tree that drops spiky seed balls."],balsam:["Thick and sweet, like vanilla, cinnamon and flat cola, with a soft warm resinous glow.","Long used in cough syrups and wound ointments, and one of the commonest triggers in skin allergy patch tests."],mastic:["Piney, clean and slightly lemony, a glassy resin note with a soft balsamic sweetness.","Often called the world's first chewing gum, it also flavours a liqueur, Turkish delight and stretchy ice cream."],copaiba:["Soft, peppery and gently woody, a mellow honeyed resin that rounds and smooths.","A golden liquid from Amazon rainforest trees, rich in beta-caryophyllene and long used as a folk remedy for wounds."],omumbiri:["Lemony and piney with fresh pepper over a soft, smoky incense warmth.","Himba women mix it into otjize, the butterfat and red ochre paste that colours their skin and hair."],breubranco:["Fresh, lemony and peppery, a bright crumbly incense note with a clean, airy lift.","A crumbly pale gum forming where insects bore into Amazon trees, burned in homes and used to caulk canoes."],opoponax:["Warm, honeyed and balsamic, softer and rounder than its bitter cousin, with a gentle powdery glow.","A gum from a Horn of Africa shrub, the gentler sister of one of the Magi's gifts, and famous in Shalimar."],copal:["Bright, lemony and piney, with a smoky edge like a ceremonial burner glowing at dusk.","Sacred to the Maya and Aztecs, it is still burned on Day of the Dead altars and in healing ceremonies."],dragonsblood:["Warm and balsamic with hints of spice and smoke, a rich, glowing ambery depth.","A deep red gum bled by umbrella-shaped trees on a remote island, used since antiquity as a dye, varnish and medicine."],ambergris:["Salty, sweet and skin-like, a radiant mineral warmth that clings like sun on bare shoulders.","Lucky beachcombers sometimes find waxy grey lumps of it, born in whale guts, though a lab molecule now stands in."],musk:["Soft, clean and powdery, a cosy glow like freshly laundered sheets against bare arms.","Once taken from a pod on a male Himalayan deer; its lab-made versions now scent most laundry detergents."],ambrette:["Soft and velvety with a pear-like, slightly winey sweetness and a warm, sensual skin glow.","A hibiscus relative in the same genus as okra, one of the rare plants giving an animal-like sensual note."],civet:["Warm, faecal and furry, a dirty animal note that makes white florals glow sensually.","Once scraped from a gland of a caged cat-like African mammal; a famous coffee passes through an Asian cousin."],hyraceum:["Fermented and animal, somewhere between leather, tobacco, musk and dark oud.","Black, resinous deposits built up over centuries in cliff crevices by a small furry mammal distantly related to elephants."],castoreum:["Dark, smoky and leathery with a sweet, almost vanilla warmth like old saddle polish.","From a dam-building rodent, it was a by-product of the fur trade and once a natural raspberry flavouring."],galaxolide:["Clean, sweet and softly floral, the cosy glow of freshly washed laundry.","A 1960s lab-made polycyclic musk, one of the most widely used aroma chemicals and found in most laundry detergents."],vanilla:["Creamy, sweet and comforting, like warm custard with a dark, slightly boozy depth.","The flavour of custard, ice cream and cola, and the second most expensive spice after saffron."],tonka:["Warm and sweet, smelling of hay, almond and soft marzipan with a hint of tobacco.","Chefs grate it like nutmeg over desserts, though its coumarin content keeps it out of food sold in America."],cacao:["Dry, bitter and roasted, like an unsweetened bar snapped open, earthy and faintly fruity.","The Aztecs drank it frothed with chilli and used it as currency; today it fills Easter eggs and truffles."],coffee:["Roasted, bitter and deep, the toasty steam of a freshly ground morning brew.","Legend says a goatherd saw his goats dancing after nibbling its red cherries; it now fills millions of morning cups."],almond:["Sweet, nutty and marzipan-like, with a cherry-stone sharpness and a soft powdery comfort.","Ground into marzipan and frangipane, and its sharp smell is the classic clue to cyanide in detective stories."],honey:["Golden, sticky and warm, with a slightly animal, tobacco-like sweetness like a waxy hive.","Made by bees from nectar and stored in waxy combs; pots found in ancient Egyptian tombs were still edible."],tobacco:["Rich, dry and honeyed, like a humidor full of dried fruit, hay and cigars.","Brought to Europe from the Americas in the sixteenth century, then rolled into cigars and packed into pipes."],rum:["Warm and boozy, with dried fruit, dark molasses and oak barrels in a sticky glow.","The sailors' and pirates' spirit, once issued daily to the Royal Navy as a tot, later mixed with lime."],hazelnut:["Roasted, buttery and nutty, like a warm praline spread with a soft toasted sweetness.","The nut in Nutella and Ferrero Rocher, from bushy shrubs whose nuts are also called cobnuts and filberts."],pistachio:["Nutty, creamy and slightly green, like a pale gelato with a soft salty edge.","A green nut in a split shell, used in baklava, Sicilian gelato and Dubai-style chocolate bars."],licorice:["Dark, sweet and anisic, like a chewy black sweet with a cool, earthy depth.","Its extract flavours Pontefract cakes and Allsorts, and contains a compound many times sweeter than sugar."],caramel:["Sticky, buttery and golden, like a pan of molten sweetness just before it burns.","Made by heating sucrose until it turns amber, it fills Twix bars and forms the syrupy topping of flan."],date:["Rich, honeyed and jammy, like sticky dried fruit with a soft, faintly smoky caramel warmth.","The sticky fruit of a desert palm, traditionally eaten to break the fast during Ramadan and served with coffee."],cognac:["Fruity, winey and boozy, a warm amber glow of oak, dried fruit and soft spice.","A double-distilled spirit aged in oak casks, sipped from a balloon glass and graded VS, VSOP or XO."],whisky:["Smoky, oaky and boozy, with peat smoke, malt sweetness and dried fruit by a fire.","Distilled from grain and aged in oak casks; some island versions taste strongly of peat smoke and iodine."],truffle:["Earthy, musky and faintly garlicky, a damp forest-floor note with a sensual, gassy depth.","Hunted underground with trained dogs or pigs in autumn woods, then shaved thinly over pasta and risotto."],chestnut:["Warm, nutty and sweet, like roasted kernels from a street brazier on a cold evening.","Roasted on an open fire in the Christmas song, sold hot in paper cones and puréed into Mont Blanc desserts."],rice:["Soft, milky and slightly nutty, like a bowl of just-cooked grains with popcorn hints.","A staple grain feeding half the world; fragrant varieties owe their popcorn-like aroma to 2-acetyl-1-pyrroline."],sugarcane:["Fresh, green and grassy, with a juicy sweetness edged by dark molasses.","A giant tropical grass, chewed raw as a snack and the source of most of the world's sucrose."],maple:["Caramelised, nutty and woody-sweet, like pancakes drizzled with something golden and steaming.","Its sweet golden product, poured over pancakes, shares a key aroma molecule, sotolon, with fenugreek seeds."],kola:["Spicy and lemony, like an ice-cold soft drink with vanilla and cinnamon prickling on the tongue.","Caffeine-rich nuts chewed across West Africa and offered to welcome guests; they gave a famous brown soft drink its name."],macadamia:["Creamy and buttery, a rich, mellow roasted nut note with a soft milky sweetness.","A rich, very hard-shelled nut native to subtropical rainforests, often paired with white chocolate in cookies."],carob:["Sweet, dark and date-like, with dusty cocoa-powder facets and a mellow molasses warmth.","Its seeds are said to have given jewellers the carat, and its ground pulp is a caffeine-free chocolate substitute."],shea:["Soft, creamy and nutty, like a rich balm melting into warm skin.","A fat from the kernels of a West African savannah tree, the base of countless hand creams and lip balms."],cashew:["Creamy, buttery and lightly roasted, a soft milky nut note with gentle sweetness.","A kidney-shaped nut hanging beneath a fleshy false fruit; its shell holds a caustic oil related to poison ivy's."],agave:["Boozy, peppery and green, with a cooked sweetness and a faint smoky edge.","A spiky succulent of arid highlands, distilled into a spirit sipped with salt and a wedge of lime."],absinthe:["Bitter, herbal and cool, with anise sweetness and a sharp grassy bite.","A potent anise spirit, banned for decades, poured over a sugar cube on a slotted spoon by Belle Epoque artists."],wine:["Fruity and dry, with red berries, grape skins and a slightly tannic, ethereal lift.","Sacramental at communion, swirled at dinner tables, and judged by sommeliers for its legs and bouquet."],marzipan:["Sweet, soft and powdery with a cherry-stone sharpness, like sugared kernels ground smooth.","Moulded into little fruits and pigs, it runs through Christmas stollen and sits under the icing on fruitcake."],tamarind:["Sour and sticky, like dates and molasses with a tangy, fruity, mouth-puckering edge.","Its sticky brown pulp gives the tang to Worcestershire sauce, HP sauce and Indian chutneys."],marshmallow:["Soft, airy and powdery, a fluffy vanillic cloud like a puffed confection toasted by a fire.","Once made from a wetland plant's sap, these spongy sweets are toasted over campfires and floated on hot cocoa."],wheat:["Dry, toasty and hay-like, like sunlit stalks at harvest time and a warm loaf.","Milled into the flour for bread, pasta and cake, its golden ears decorate harvest festivals."],cottoncandy:["Fluffy, caramelised and jammy, like a cloud of melted sweets with a berry edge.","Heated sucrose whirled into fine threads around a stick at funfairs; one of its inventors was, ironically, a dentist."],champagne:["Crisp, effervescent and faintly bready, with bright fruity bubbles and a chilled, celebratory lift.","Popped at weddings and New Year and sprayed from podiums by racing drivers, it gets its bubbles in the bottle."],sake:["Soft, milky and faintly boozy, with hints of apple, banana and cooked grain.","A clear brewed drink made with koji mould, served warm or chilled in small ceramic cups."],coumarin:["Warm and sweet, smelling of freshly cut hay, almond and soft vanilla.","The molecule behind the smell of new-mown hay and sweet woodruff, also present in cassia cinnamon and tonka beans."],barley:["Toasted, bready and dry, like warm biscuits with hay and a hint of brewing grain.","Germinated, kiln-dried and mashed, this cereal is the backbone of beer and whisky, and thickens hearty broths."],milk:["Soft, creamy and lightly sweet, a comforting dairy smoothness like a soothing bedtime cup.","Poured on breakfast cereal and into tea, it is the very first food of every newborn mammal."],whippedcream:["Light, airy and dairy-sweet, a fluffy soft cloud with a vanillic touch.","Beaten until fluffy and piped onto trifles and hot chocolate, or squirted from an aerosol can."],macaron:["Sweet, powdery and nutty, like crisp sugary shells around a soft, chewy centre.","Pastel-coloured shells sandwiched with ganache, stacked in towers in the windows of smart patisseries."],bread:["Warm, yeasty and golden, like a loaf just pulled from the oven.","A staple risen with yeast and sliced for sandwiches; charred remains of a flat version predate farming by millennia."],seasalt:["Breezy and briny, like ocean spray drying on sun-warmed skin with a cool ozonic tang.","Harvested from evaporating seaside pans and flaked over food; in perfume a melon-tinged molecule evokes the ocean."],seaweed:["Dark, iodic and briny, like rock pools at low tide on a grey morning.","Gathered on rocky shores for food, fertiliser and hot baths; bladderwrack and kelp are common kinds."],driftwood:["Dry, sun-bleached and salt-scoured, a pale timber note carried on a cool sea breeze.","Silvery branches and logs tossed ashore by the tide, collected by beachcombers for bonfires and decor."],samphire:["Green, salty and spicy, like fleshy shoots picked on a sea cliff in the spray.","A fleshy cliff plant pickled and eaten for centuries; Shakespeare called gathering it on cliff faces a dreadful trade."],flint:["Dry, cool and metallic with a hint of spark, like two pebbles knocked together.","Knapped into prehistoric axes, it later sparked muskets and lighters, and lies in dark nodules within chalk cliffs."],sand:["Sun-baked, dry and softly salty, like tiny grains clinging to skin after a seaside afternoon.","Made of tiny grains of eroded rock, it fills hourglasses and children's buckets and is melted into glass."]};export{e as CLUES};
